xtend.\n\nReason:\nI choose **N: g8-f6** because:\n- It develops a piece toward the center following opening principles\n- It attacks White's advanced g4 pawn, creating an immediate tactical threat\n- It prepares kingside castling\n- The knight on f6 is a flexible, strong square that controls key central squares (e4, d5)\n- It doesn't commit to any pawn structure prematurely and keeps my options open\n\nAnswer: N: g8-f6"}
