gest move because:\n- It develops a piece with tempo (threatens the pinned Bishop)\n- Creates a pin: the d2 Bishop cannot move without exposing the King to check\n- Forces White to deal with the pin (possibly a3 or Nc3 blocking)\n- Follows classical opening principles: develop pieces, control the center, and create threats\n- Puts immediate tactical pressure on White's somewhat uncastled and exposed position\n\nAnswer: B: f8-b4"}
