hat out of play. I should exploit White's exposed King position.\n\nReason: **Q: d8-h4** is the strongest move because:\n- It attacks the vulnerable g4 pawn and threatens the uncastled White King\n- It creates immediate tactical threats that White must address\n- The Queen on h4 coordinates well with potential future attacks\n- It exploits White's King safety issues before they can castle\n- Forces White into a defensive posture rather than allowing them to coordinate an attack with their advanced Queen\n\nAnswer: Q: d8-h4"}
