rful attack - it forks the knight on b1 and threatens the White king's position since the king has already moved and appears vulnerable. This tactical blow could win material.\n\nReason: B: a5-c3 is the strongest move because it creates an immediate tactical threat by attacking the undefended knight on b1. White will be forced to deal with this threat, and I can win the knight or force significant concessions. This is much more forcing than merely chasing the queen with B: a5-b6.\n\nAnswer: B: a5-c3"}
