 excellent outpost on d5, where it cannot be easily driven away by pawns. From d5, the knight controls many key squares (c3, e3, f4, b4, c7, e7), puts pressure on White's position, and supports potential future attacks. The knight is well-protected and creates both tactical and positional threats against White's somewhat exposed king position.\n\nAnswer: N: e3-d5"}
