otential back rank issues, but not immediately addressing the position.\n\nReason: The knight on f2 is already deep in White's position but needs better placement. **N: f2-e4** is the strongest move because:\n- It centralizes my knight to an excellent outpost\n- Controls critical central squares\n- The knight on e4 is difficult to dislodge\n- It supports both my advanced pawns (e5, f5) and provides defensive coverage\n- From e4, the knight can potentially jump to d6, f6, or g5 in future moves\n\nAnswer: N: f2-e4"}
