 c5, e5)\n- Coordinates well with my rooks\n- Prepares potential threats against White's exposed king\n\n**Reason:**\nN: f2-d3 is the best move because it maximizes the knight's influence in the center while maintaining all my tactical advantages. From d3, the knight controls critical squares and can quickly reposition to support my rooks or attack White's weak pawns. This centralization, combined with my material advantage, should lead to a winning position.\n\n**Answer:** N: f2-d3"}
