awn on e3 is my most powerful asset. Pushing it to e2 creates an immediate promotion threat that White cannot ignore. After e3-e2, White will be forced to deal with this pawn, and if White doesn't capture it immediately (which would require moving the King from e1), I promote to a Queen on my next turn, gaining a decisive material advantage. This is a forcing move that puts maximum pressure on White.\n\nAnswer: P: e3-e2"}
