esn't address immediate threats.\n\nReason: The move **R: e8-e3** is the strongest because it places my rook on a dominating square on the third rank, attacks horizontally across the board, and most importantly, it supports my incredibly dangerous passed pawn on e2. With the rook on e3, I'm threatening to push the pawn to e1 for promotion on the next move, and the rook defends/supports this plan while also putting pressure on White's exposed king position. This creates immediate tactical threats that White must address.\n\nAnswer: R: e8-e3"}
