\n1 |    |    |    |    |    |    |    |    | 1\n  +----+----+----+----+----+----+----+----+\n     a    b    c    d    e    f    g    h \nYour valid moves are (src-dst-promotion, or src-dst):\n[P: a7-a5, P: a7-a6, R: a8-b8, R: a8-c8, R: a8-d8, R: a8-e8, R: a8-f8, P: b7-b5, P: b7-b6, P: c7-c5, P: c7-c6, P: g5-g4, K: g8-f7, K: g8-f8, K: g8-g7, K: g8-h7, K: g8-h8, P: h6-h5]\nYour answer format should be: Answer: piece-name: move. \nPiece-name and move (src-dst-promotion or src-dst) should be directly copied EXACTLY from valid move list.\nExample of valid output format: N: a1-b3; P: e7-e8-q; Piece B: g5-f4.\nPlease select a move from your valid moves that maximize your probability of winning.\n', 'reasoning': '', 'output': "Situation: I'm playing as Black in an endgame position. Material count shows Black has: 1 Rook (a8), 1 King (g8), and 5 Pawns (a7, b7, c7, g5, h6). White has: 1 King (f5) and 1 Pawn (a3). Black has a significant material advantage with a rook and extra pawns.\n\nThe White King is actively placed on f5, relatively centralized and close to my king on g8. My rook on a8 is currently passive on the back rank. The key to winning this position is to activate my rook to cut off the White King, while advancing my pawns to create passed pawns.\n\nEvaluation:\n1. **R: a8-f8** - Activates the rook to the f-file, giving check to the White King on f5. This forces the White King to move and allows me to seize the initiative. The rook becomes active and can control key files.\n\n2. **R: a8-e8** - Activates the rook to the e-file, centralizing it. This is also strong but doesn't give immediate check.\n\n3. **P: g5-g4** - Advances a passed pawn, but this allows the White King to potentially capture it or block it effectively.\n\n4. **K: g8-f7** - Activates my king, but this is slow and doesn't address the need to activate my rook first.\n\nReason: **R: a8-f8** is the strongest move. It gives check, forcing White's king to retreat or move to a less active square. After the check, I can use my rook actively to support my pawn advances, cut off the White King, and convert my material advantage into a win. Activating the rook with tempo (check) is the most forcing and efficient way to take control of the position.\n\nAnswer: R: a8-f8"}
