 standard technique of using checks to restrict the opponent's king's mobility\n\nReason: In Queen vs King endgames, the winning technique involves giving checks to drive the opposing king to the edge of the board, then coordinating the queen and king to deliver checkmate. Since the White King is already on the back rank, d7-d8 gives check and maintains maximum control, forcing the White King into an even more restricted position. This is the most direct path to checkmate.\n\nAnswer: Q: d7-d8"}
